  "result": "I added `compareVersions` to `src/cli/semver.ts` and committed it. `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **Behavior:** it compares dotted versions part by part as numbers, so `1.10.0` is greater than `1.9.0`. Missing parts count as 0, so `1.2` equals `1.2.0`. It returns -1, 0 or 1. It throws `Invalid version` if any part isn't purely digits.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/semver.test.ts` covers equality, numeric ordering, versions of different length, and invalid input. I added a weight for it in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Plan notes:** these are in `.krn/runs/fr40-agent/notes.md`, which is git-ignored. I wrote the plan before coding and marked it done at the end.\n- **Commit title:** the convention asks for the task id in parentheses at the end, but I wasn't given one. The commit is `27cf2c5 Add compareVersions for dotted numeric versions` with no id. If you give me the id, I can amend the title.",
